WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Priya Nair: Okay, let's start. This is the weekly sync for the Q3 onboarding redesign. On the call we have me, Marcus, Devon, and Sarah from support.

2
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Priya Nair: First item, the new user checklist. Marcus, where are we on the checklist component?

3
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:48.000
Marcus Chen: It's in review. The design is done and I agreed with Devon that we ship it behind a feature flag first. We decided to roll it out to 10% of new signups starting next Monday instead of 100%, so we can watch error rates.

4
00:00:48.500 --> 00:01:05.000
Priya Nair: Good, that's safer. Marcus, can you own the feature flag rollout? I need that done by September 5th.

5
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:12.000
Marcus Chen: Yes, I'll own the rollout. I will have the flag configured and the 10% cohort live by September 5th.

6
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:31.000
Devon Ruiz: On my side, the onboarding emails are still blocked on copy. Sarah, do you have the final subject lines from support feedback?

7
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:47.000
Sarah Kim: Almost. I'm compiling the top five complaints from last month's tickets. I will send the subject line doc to Devon by Wednesday, September 3rd.

8
00:01:47.500 --> 00:02:02.000
Devon Ruiz: Perfect. Once I have that, I will finalize the email sequence and send it to Priya for approval by September 8th.

9
00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:20.000
Priya Nair: Great. Second item. We agreed last week to cut the onboarding survey from seven questions down to three. Did we finalize which three?

10
00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:38.000
Marcus Chen: Yes, we decided on: how did you hear about us, what's your primary use case, and company size. We dropped the NPS question from onboarding entirely and moved it to day 30 instead.

11
00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:50.000
Priya Nair: Agreed, that's final. Devon, can you update the survey config and remove the old questions by Friday?

12
00:02:50.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Devon Ruiz: Sure, I'll have the survey updated by Friday, September 5th.

13
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:18.000
Sarah Kim: One more thing from support. We're seeing a spike in tickets about the password reset flow timing out. It's not part of this project but it's urgent. Fourteen tickets this week alone.

14
00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:34.000
Priya Nair: That sounds like a bug, not onboarding scope. Let's flag it. Marcus, can you file a ticket with the platform team today and loop in Sarah?

15
00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:40.000
Marcus Chen: Will do, I'll file that today and copy Sarah on it.

16
00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:58.000
Priya Nair: Okay, last item. Budget. We agreed to hold off on paid user research until Q4. We will not spend the $4,000 research budget this quarter. That's confirmed.

17
00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:15.000
Priya Nair: Risk to flag: if Sarah's subject line doc slips past Wednesday, the email sequence deadline of September 8th is at risk too, since Devon is blocked on it.

18
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:30.000
Devon Ruiz: Agreed, that's the critical path. I'll ping Sarah on Tuesday if I haven't seen it yet.

19
00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:45.000
Priya Nair: Sounds good. To summarize: Marcus owns the feature flag rollout by September 5th and the platform bug ticket today. Devon owns the survey config by September 5th and the email sequence by September 8th, pending Sarah's copy. Sarah owns the subject line doc by September 3rd.

20
00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:58.000
Priya Nair: We decided to hold research spend until Q4, and we decided to launch the checklist at 10% first, not 100%. Next sync same time next week. Thanks everyone.

21
00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:05.000
Marcus Chen: Sounds good, thanks all.

22
00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:08.000
Sarah Kim: Bye everyone.
